(begin-tx "ATS-I24 — INFO_ATS|UpgradeBranding quote vs measured charge")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [ATS-I24 · 01 · buy branding months for an ATS pair] ---")
;;FUNCTION COVERAGE (G6) — `INFO_ATS|UpgradeBranding`, per the owner's spec: an INFO_ must report the same cost
;;the op actually charges. Template and rationale: `modules/ATS.repl <<ATS-I1>>`.
;;A STOA-ONLY OP: the preview quotes zero IGNIS and a real STOA figure, so BOTH halves are asserted
;;— an IGNIS-only test would pass on a preview that had lost the STOA leg entirely, which is exactly
;;the defect found in three other previews tonight.
;;The managed caps sit at TRANSACTION TOP LEVEL and are written out literally: `env-sigs` from inside
;;a `let` sets signatures without INSTALLING managed caps, and a `map`-built list does not install
;;them either. Both traps are documented at <<ATS-I2>>.
;;THE CLOCK IS THE FIXTURE. `BRD|C>UPGRADE` refuses while more than 15 days of Blue Flag remain
;;(`04_BRD.pact:266`), and this entity's branding was already bought earlier in the chain. Rather
;;than hunt for an un-upgraded entity — which would make the block depend on which suites ran —
;;the clock is moved past the expiry and put back. `rollback-tx` does NOT undo `env-chain-data`,
;;so the restore below is mandatory, not tidiness.
(env-chain-data { "block-time": (time "2030-11-22T00:00:00Z") })
(env-sigs
  [ { "key": "PK_AOZ", "caps": [] }
    { "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }
