(begin-tx "ATS-I32 — INFO_ATS|Issue: both currencies measured")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [ATS-I32 · 01 · issue a fresh autostake pair] ---")
;;FUNCTION COVERAGE (G6) — `INFO_ATS|Issue`, per the owner's spec. Template: <<ATS-I1>>.
;;BOTH currencies are asserted; an IGNIS-only test passes just as well on a preview that lost its STOA
;;leg, which is exactly what happened to three other previews in this suite.
;;
;;ARITY DIVERGENCE — the preview takes 3 arguments (`patron account ats-names`), the exec takes 8.
;;Everything the exec adds is per-pair CONFIGURATION (decimals, reward token, its NFR flag, the
;;reward-bearing token, its NFR flag); none of it reaches the price, which is amount-independent and
;;scales only with the NUMBER of pairs. That is the claim this block settles.
;;
;;THE REAL BLOCKER WAS THE RBT, not the pair name. `UEV_IssueData` (`08_ATS.pact:2396`) runs
;;`DPTF::CAP_Owner reward-bearing-token` — so the RBT must be an EXISTING DPTF the caller owns — and
;;then refuses any token already serving as an RT or RBT elsewhere. Every AOZT-owned DPTF on this
;;chain is already spoken for (PKOSON/EKOSON/AKOSON are PlebeicStrength's reward tokens, TKRBT is
;;TestKickPair's). So a virgin one is issued first — the same pattern that unlocked <<ATS-I31>>'s coil
;;fixture and three AQP blocks before it.
;;Both setup and measured ops charge STOA; the caps are declared at TRANSACTION TOP LEVEL and written
;;out literally (the two install traps are documented at <<ATS-I2>>), sized generously because the
;;point of the block is to MEASURE the charge rather than to presume it.
(env-sigs
  [ { "key": "PK_AOZ", "caps": [] }
    { "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }
    { "key": "95a59029029524ebb250b2fafe6826ff88bb59c527d661cba3279d09a51d3bdf"
    , "caps":
      [
