;;`ATSU|C>X_KICKSTART` (`10_ATSU.pact:377`) enforces `(= index -1.0)` — kickstarting is the act that
;;gives a pair its first index, so it is reachable exactly once per pair, at birth. `TestKickPair`
;;exists for this and `[6.6]` already spent it, which is what the label recorded. But a pair issued
;;HERE is born at -1 like any other, so the op is not unreachable — the standing state was.
