(begin-tx "ATSU-G1 — the recoverer gate, bracketed from both sides")
(print "")
(print "=== ATSU-G1 — ATSU|C>COLD_RECOVERY =========================================")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;`ATSU|C>COLD_RECOVERY` carries `CAP_EnforceAccountOwnership recoverer` and had never refused
;;anybody. Witnessing it needs care, because an ordinary stranger NEVER REACHES IT: `10_ATSU.pact:497`
;;runs an `enforce-one` over five guards -- DALOS admin, ATSU admin, the account's own guard, its
;;SOVEREIGN's and its GOVERNOR's -- and that refuses a stranger first, with a message about ledger
;;permissions that says nothing about the recoverer.
;;
;;So the gate is shadowed by a BROADER check, and the only caller who can reach it is one who already
;;passed that check while not being the recoverer. The Demiurgoi admin is exactly that caller. The
;;three assertions below bracket the gate: the first lands short of it, the second ON it, the third
;;past it.
;;
;;ANHD IS THE ATTACKER HERE, deliberately and unusually. Everywhere else in this suite that would be
;;the wrong choice -- ANHD owns the fixtures, so a refusal would be unattributable. Here it is the
;;ONLY choice that works: the attack is precisely "the most privileged key in the system still cannot
;;recover on somebody else's behalf", and no lesser key gets far enough to ask the question.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-ATS:module{AutostakeV3} ATS)
        (ref-TS01-C2:module{TalosStageOne_ClientTwoV2} TS01-C2)
        (pair:string "Auryndex-98c486052a51")
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<ATSU-G1>> the pair has cold recovery ON, so the op is live"
                true (ref-ATS::UR_ToggleColdRecovery pair))
            ;;SHORT OF THE GATE. A stranger is turned away by the ledger-permission `enforce-one`,
            ;;whose message concerns the ACCOUNT, not the recoverer. Pinned to document that the
            ;;obvious attack does not witness this gate at all.
            (expect-failure "<<ATSU-G1>> SHADOW: a stranger is stopped by the ledger-permission check, never reaching the recoverer gate"
                "Invalid permission for normalizing ATS|Ledger Account Operations"
                (ref-TS01-C2::ATS|C_ColdRecovery KST.EMMA KST.ANHD pair 1.0))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-C2:module{TalosStageOne_ClientTwoV2} TS01-C2)
        (pair:string "Auryndex-98c486052a51")
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;ON THE GATE. The Demiurgoi master key satisfies the `enforce-one` as DALOS admin, so
            ;;the ledger check is out of the way -- and the refusal now names the RECOVERER's key,
            ;;which is the only thing `CAP_EnforceAccountOwnership recoverer` can be.
            (expect-failure "<<ATSU-G1>> GATE: even the admin cannot cold-recover on someone else's behalf"
                "Keyset failure (keys-all): [PK_Emma...]"
                (ref-TS01-C2::ATS|C_ColdRecovery KST.ANHD KST.EMMA pair 1.0))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
